# Analyze why NQ one-bar 50-breakout underperformed in 2026 (as of 2026-07-14)

Execute complete empirical diagnostics, NOT strategy tuning. Repo /home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research. ChatGPT research lead independently verifies. Scope: frozen exact one-bar 50-complete-30m-bar long+short NQ-equivalent strategy. Source: 1-minute Dukascopy USATECH BID CFD proxy 2013-01-01 through 2026-07-14; NOT CME NQ. Original strategy and native ML4T backtest artifacts MUST NOT CHANGE. No live orders, no commits/push, no holdout access after 2026-07-14.

Before substantial work inspect branch/HEAD/remotes, git status and existing tmux/Codex sessions. Read AGENTS.md/nested instructions, docs/research_sessions.md, promote/one_bar_nq_30m/strategy.yaml, README, config/backtest.yaml, latest report/tearsheet metrics, annual trial evidence and run_log/validation_status.json. Preserve all dirty and unrelated work. Read FULL installed local ML4T skills SKILL.md matching regime-awareness, non-stationarity, drift-detection, polars-patterns, regime-features, calendar-ops, tearsheet, causal-identification, lookahead-bias; verify actual ml4t diagnostic/engineer APIs. Do NOT handroll backtest or customize original strategy. Use ml4t.diagnostic/engineer where applicable, Polars for ledger aggregations and causal trailing features, native ml4t.backtest previously ran and results are frozen.

Research question: What MEASURABLE mechanisms explain full-tick net -$14,166.96 in Jan1-Jul14 2026 for 238 trades, versus long-history +$166,107.92/5462 and prior 2018-2025 strong trend? Separate source/execution artifact from actual economic change. Historic zero cost 2026 -$10,806.96, costed -$14,166.96 so it ALREADY loses without costs. No ex-post rule tuning.

Predeclare diagnostic scope and bins IN A NEW manifest before inspecting the metrics:
A. Accounting: per month of 2026 Jan-Jul14, trade count, gross zero-cost/costed net, long vs short, exit reason STOP vs MARKET, winrate, win/loss size, profit factor, daily drawdown. Compare Jan-Jul14 slices of each prior year (not full-year 2025), plus baseline 2018-25 H1 and 2021-25 H1. Split RTH 09:30-16 Chicago vs overnight (entry_timestamp local DST) as pure attribution. Concentration best/worst 1,3,5,10 trade PnL and stop gap through. Compare losses in 2026 by month and event type; isolate macro date windows only descriptively.
B. Edge/false breaks: using underlying canonical 1m BID data, build causal 30m complete prior-bar levels exactly matching existing strategy, match entry_context/trade CSVs. For trade at time t, compute price (index-point and ATR-normalized) move from entry to next observed opening price, favorable excursion/adverse excursion, stop hit rate, time exits, breakout distance from 50-bar high/low and market gaps. 1m OHLC cannot determine intraminute ordering; report unknown. Inspect entry_context available fields first and join only if valid; be precise on handling lookahead: trailing ATR, prior 20-bar return, prior 20-bar trend efficiency, realized vol, 50-bar channel width known at entry from completed PREVIOUS bars; next-bar reversal/MAE ARE outcomes used only descriptively, NEVER for signals/trade selection.
C. Structural market regime using 30m OHLC reconstructed with existing validated bar builder: trailing ATR20 in points and bps; 20bar efficiency ratio = abs(close[-1]-close[-21])/sum(abs(close change)) trailing; prior bar range relative ATR; 50bar channel range; vol percentiles from PAST 252 or 500 complete bars, not full-history percentile; daily market close-to-close realized vol as diagnostic. Compare 2026 vs historical via distributions and KS/PSI (from installed ml4t.diagnostic if usable) and conditional profitability by PREDEFINED terciles based on 2018-2025 reference thresholds; make thresholds descriptive, not approved filters.
D. Hypotheses: trend failure/whipsaw vs stop-out jump vs volatility compression vs disproportionate overnight churn vs adverse side asymmetry. Test hypothesis ordering using A-C, not news narratives. No optimization, no regime filter added, no ML predictive performance claim. Note possible bias from yearly resets, exact one-bar next-open absent data, OCO non-atomic. Use static comparison of fixed strategy, not rerun parameter grid.
E. External public CONTEMPORANEOUS market context only through 2026-07-14: cite first-party Nasdaq official Feb 2026 NDX -2.3% AI disruption tariff (https://www.nasdaq.com/articles/global-indexes/index-monthly-scorecard-february-2026), April 2026 NDX +15.6% after March geopolitical Iran ceasefire (https://www.nasdaq.com/articles/global-indexes/monthly-scorecard-april-2026), May 2026 NDX +10.5% and AI optimism (https://www.nasdaq.com/articles/global-indexes/monthly-scorecard-may-2026), Cboe June 2026 falling megacap MGTN -9.2%, Russell2000 +3.6%, VIX 15.3 to 16.5, stock dispersion/rotation (https://www.cboe.com/insights/posts/index-insights-june-2026/), Cboe January 2026 early rotation (https://www.cboe.com/insights/posts/index-insights-january-2026/); FRED https://fred.stlouisfed.org/data/VXNCLS for optional implied vol Jan-Jul14 ONLY if local canonical time series available or truly needed. Do not include news from AFTER Jul14 in Jan-Jul attribution. Explain broad NDX may surge in April/May while strategy loses due to intraday breakout horizon; outside reporting does NOT explain strategy PnL unless matched to loss timing. Label event correlations as HYPOTHESIS.

Use Python/Polars via installed env and ml4t diagnostic/engineering for features, tests; use tmux for long data calculations if needed, first check existing tmux and avoid duplicates. Optimize memory: source is 3.88m rows 163 Parquet partitions, filter 2018 onward if prior-study sufficient (sample 2013-2026 already available), scan lazily and only needed OHLC fields. Do not download data or read after Jul14. Do not create huge sub-minute ML feature matrix unnecessarily. No return computation with future data for features, no protected holdout.

