+def render_report(metrics: dict, monthly: pl.DataFrame, regimes: pl.DataFrame,
+                  breakdowns: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> str:
+    a = metrics["accounting"]
+    lines = ["# Why the fixed one-bar strategy lost money in 2026", "",
+             "**Review type:** historical descriptive review. **Decision:** the package remains `EXPLORATORY` and `NOT_APPROVED`. No strategy rule changed. The backtest did not run again.", "",
+             "## Finding", "",
+             f"The frozen 2026 ledger has {a['2026_trades']} trades. It lost **${a['full_tick_net_pnl_usd']:,.2f} net** with full-tick costs and **${a['zero_cost_pnl_usd']:,.2f} in the separate zero-cost run**. The loss is therefore present before costs. The full-tick result is ${a['zero_cost_to_full_tick_net_difference_usd']:,.2f} below the zero-cost result. The costed `gross_pnl` field is before commissions but already includes fill slippage; do not read it as zero-cost PnL.", "",
+             "The strongest verified explanation is weak realized breakout payoff across this observed 2026 sample, with negative PnL already before modeled costs. Shorts lost most of the total. The strategy recorded stop fills on 44 trades, but every trade-ledger `exit_reason` is `signal`; the native `fills.csv` order type is required to separate protective STOP fills from market time exits. Source bars show 49 post-entry 1-minute OHLC touches of the nominal 50-point stop level. The five-touch difference may include minute-path ambiguity or unmatched triggers. Costs widen the loss. These observations do not identify a macro cause.", "",
+             "## Monthly attribution", "",
+             "| Month | Trades | Costed gross before commission | Full-tick net | Zero-cost net | Win rate | STOP exits |",
+             "|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|"]
